WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.730
<b>Adventurers' Guild</b>

00:00.870 --> 00:04.740
That's 12,000 gold for the magic 
stones you brought in today.

00:05.040 --> 00:07.350
Thanks for always helping me out, Natalie.

00:07.620 --> 00:11.690
The Snack Slimes you came 
up with sold out again.

00:13.060 --> 00:18.570
Maybe you'd make more money selling 
sweets than killing slimes.

00:18.570 --> 00:22.500
Nah, I'm not trying to 
get rich or anything.

00:22.500 --> 00:23.710
Oh, right.

00:23.990 --> 00:25.830
This letter came for you.

00:25.830 --> 00:27.210
I wonder who it's from...

00:30.660 --> 00:33.320
Ooh, I didn't know this was a thing!

00:33.320 --> 00:34.400
Never heard of it.

00:34.400 --> 00:36.050
What does it say?

00:36.330 --> 00:39.510
It's a notice about the 
World Spirit Summit!

00:48.610 --> 00:59.620
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

02:10.530 --> 02:13.480
World Spirit Summit?

02:13.730 --> 02:18.810
Spirits from all over the world gather on 
the bank of Nanterre Lake, apparently.

02:15.530 --> 02:18.330
<b>We Searched for an Undead</b>

02:18.810 --> 02:21.480
Big Sister and I were invited.

02:21.480 --> 02:24.910
You two are slime spirits, after all.

02:24.910 --> 02:28.130
Just hearing the word 
"summit" makes me tired.

02:28.130 --> 02:31.940
Will they have an all-you-can-drink 
party after it's over?!

02:31.940 --> 02:34.720
Uh, first of all, you're not a spirit.

02:35.950 --> 02:37.960
I wanna go!

02:37.960 --> 02:39.080
Me, too.

02:39.080 --> 02:43.470
As your mother, I'd be worried 
to send you two kids alone.

02:43.740 --> 02:45.880
Then you can come with us!

02:45.880 --> 02:48.480
It says accompaniment by 
a guardian is permitted.

02:48.480 --> 02:49.460
Oh?

02:49.460 --> 02:52.600
Well, the three of us can make 
a relaxing trip of it, then.

02:55.820 --> 02:58.150
Yay! A trip! A trip!

02:58.150 --> 02:59.940
A trip with Mama!

02:59.940 --> 03:01.940
Shalsha, are you sleepy?

03:01.940 --> 03:04.950
I was so excited about today 
that I couldn't sleep.

03:04.950 --> 03:08.240
<i>Just like a kid the night 
before a field trip...</i>

03:11.780 --> 03:14.340
You both packed your bags pretty full, huh?

03:14.710 --> 03:17.470
Well, we'll be meeting all 
kinds of different spirits!

03:17.470 --> 03:19.330
We prepared as necessary.

03:19.330 --> 03:22.600
Oh, yeah? I wonder what's in them...

03:22.600 --> 03:24.190
That's a secret!

03:33.310 --> 03:34.610
Ta-da!

03:34.610 --> 03:37.360
Mama's special egg sandwiches!

03:38.610 --> 03:40.800
Let's eat!

03:43.760 --> 03:45.370
Yummy!

03:45.650 --> 03:49.570
Eggs from chickens raised 
in the highlands of Flatta

03:49.570 --> 03:52.880
have a rich flavor and a 
fluffy, pulpy texture.

03:52.880 --> 03:56.370
I'm glad you both seem to like them.

04:15.920 --> 04:16.990
There.

04:16.990 --> 04:18.800
Thanks, Mama!

04:18.800 --> 04:19.950
Thank you.

04:34.420 --> 04:36.290
<b>Nanterre Lake</b>

04:36.280 --> 04:38.790
Ooh, it's so pretty!

04:39.400 --> 04:43.260
They say Nanterre Lake was 
formed a few millennia ago,

04:43.260 --> 04:47.670
when rainwater filled up a hole created 
by Blue Dragon siblings fighting.

04:48.030 --> 04:50.170
What a nice view!

04:50.170 --> 04:54.150
Wait... This is where the 
summit is, right?

04:54.150 --> 04:56.560
This says it'll be held at night.

04:56.560 --> 05:00.030
Then I guess we can relax 
until the sun goes down.

05:12.700 --> 05:14.160
Honestly...

05:14.160 --> 05:16.440
These adorable daughters of mine...

05:29.240 --> 05:31.020
Falfa! Shalsha!

05:37.930 --> 05:40.510
Oh, wow!

05:40.510 --> 05:42.200
Those are spirits?

05:42.200 --> 05:45.260
That many of them show up for this?

05:46.290 --> 05:48.950
Good evening! My name's Falfa!

05:48.950 --> 05:50.300
She's quick!

05:50.300 --> 05:53.240
That daughter of mine has <i>some</i> 
communication skills...

05:57.040 --> 05:59.440
Would you like me to go with you?

06:00.710 --> 06:04.620
Oh, my! That's the rumor you 
heard? Is it really true?

06:04.620 --> 06:07.710
U-Um... Good evening.

06:07.710 --> 06:09.680
<i>You got this, Shalsha!</i>

06:09.680 --> 06:12.430
Oh, how cute! Who might you be?

06:12.430 --> 06:16.940
I'm Shalsha the slime spirit. 
This is my first time here.

06:16.940 --> 06:19.020
<i>A kid with business cards?!</i>

06:19.260 --> 06:22.500
These are sweets called "Snack Slimes."

06:22.500 --> 06:24.520
Please accept them as a 
token of friendship.

06:24.520 --> 06:26.280
<i>She brought them gifts, too?!</i>

06:26.280 --> 06:29.090
<i>So that's what was in her bag!</i>

06:29.530 --> 06:33.320
Oh, how lovely. 
Welcome to the spirit gathering.

06:33.320 --> 06:35.070
I am a waterfall spirit.

06:35.070 --> 06:37.040
I'm a volcanic ash spirit.

06:37.400 --> 06:39.780
I'm a cumulonimbus cloud spirit.

06:40.080 --> 06:42.410
I'm Shalsha's mother.

06:42.410 --> 06:44.610
I'm Azusa, the Witch of the Highlands.

06:44.610 --> 06:45.250
Nice to mee—

06:45.250 --> 06:46.910
Witch of the Highlands?!

06:46.910 --> 06:50.200
The rumor was true?! 
The Witch of the Highlands really exists?!

06:50.610 --> 06:54.430
The one they say annihilated the 
Blue Dragons <i>and</i> the demons?!

06:54.430 --> 06:57.180
I heard she's practically a god!

06:57.180 --> 06:59.270
Wait, that's super embellished!

06:59.270 --> 07:00.880
I didn't annihilate anyone!

07:00.880 --> 07:02.940
In fact, I'm very good 
friends with all of them!

07:03.440 --> 07:06.120
So the rumors are <i>almost</i> true...

07:06.120 --> 07:10.690
Speaking of rumors, is that one about 
the settlement to the south true?

07:10.960 --> 07:14.300
The one that says they never age?

07:14.300 --> 07:17.190
I heard they're not dead, 
but also not alive.

07:17.190 --> 07:18.490
Yes, that's right!

07:18.490 --> 07:22.290
I also heard they smell so horrible that 
they need perfumes to cover it up!

07:22.290 --> 07:25.790
Okay, you like rumors a little too much.

07:31.580 --> 07:34.790
That's odd. 
The summit still hasn't started.

07:34.790 --> 07:37.680
Well, let's chat again sometime.

07:37.680 --> 07:40.670
We'll have some new topics 
to talk about by then.

07:40.670 --> 07:42.560
Until next time!

07:42.820 --> 07:43.680
Huh?

07:43.680 --> 07:45.140
Farewell!

07:55.270 --> 07:57.070
It's over already?

08:09.490 --> 08:12.770
What did you think of the 
World Spirit Summit?

08:13.000 --> 08:15.380
<i>Was</i> there a summit?

08:15.380 --> 08:17.380
Yes, of course.

08:17.650 --> 08:20.600
But everyone just stood around chatting.

08:20.600 --> 08:27.600
The World Spirit Summit is when 
spirits come together just to talk.

08:27.600 --> 08:28.590
Oh...

08:28.590 --> 08:33.500
I got to talk to lots of different spirits! 
It was so much fun!

08:33.500 --> 08:37.000
I was hoping it would be 
more like an actual summit.

08:37.000 --> 08:38.850
Ah, yes...

08:38.850 --> 08:41.900
It was a proper summit a long time ago,

08:41.900 --> 08:44.720
but spirits who weren't interested 
in that stopped coming,

08:44.720 --> 08:46.990
so we gave up on the summit.

08:47.280 --> 08:49.780
That's a novel way to solve that problem.

08:49.780 --> 08:51.710
And... you are?

08:51.710 --> 08:54.900
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

08:54.900 --> 08:57.700
I'm Yufufu, a droplet spirit.

08:57.700 --> 09:00.460
I'm the one who sent the invitations.

09:00.460 --> 09:02.460
Droplet spirit?

09:02.460 --> 09:03.780
Yes.

09:03.780 --> 09:06.850
I heard there'd be cute slime spirits here,

09:06.850 --> 09:09.240
and I just had to meet them.

09:09.680 --> 09:11.910
It's getting late now.

09:11.910 --> 09:14.770
Would you like to come to my house?

09:14.770 --> 09:17.110
Huh? But we couldn't...

09:17.110 --> 09:19.370
There's no need to hold back.

09:34.120 --> 09:35.800
Here. Hot honey water.

09:36.120 --> 09:38.490
Oh, thank you.

09:38.490 --> 09:41.440
No need to speak so formally.

09:41.440 --> 09:44.290
You've lived for a long time 
yourself, haven't you?

09:44.290 --> 09:46.940
Uh, yeah. Thanks.

09:50.210 --> 09:52.690
<i>It feels like being back home.</i>

09:52.690 --> 09:54.410
The truth is...

09:54.410 --> 09:59.840
I sent those invitations because 
I'm interested in you, as well.

09:59.840 --> 10:00.620
Huh?

10:01.240 --> 10:03.400
You live a pleasant life in the highlands

10:03.400 --> 10:07.830
with lots of girls you've 
taken in as family, right?

10:08.780 --> 10:13.330
You are the central figure in your family, 
the one all others rely on.

10:13.660 --> 10:19.970
But there's no one that you can 
fully lean on yourself, is there?

10:20.430 --> 10:24.340
I mean, yeah, it is kind 
of rough sometimes...

10:24.670 --> 10:30.190
Yes. You have always put your family first.

10:30.590 --> 10:36.200
So you also need a mom 
that you can lean on.

10:36.990 --> 10:41.170
Azusa, you've done a wonderful 
job caring for your family.

10:43.190 --> 10:44.250
Mom...

10:55.490 --> 10:58.120
Yufufu... Mom?

10:59.040 --> 11:00.770
Morning, Mama!

10:59.040 --> 11:00.770
Morning, Mother.

11:00.770 --> 11:02.160
Morning.

11:02.800 --> 11:04.480
Mother, your...

11:04.480 --> 11:05.420
What happened?

11:05.420 --> 11:06.420
Huh?

11:08.090 --> 11:10.200
Wait, what?! What's going on?!

11:10.200 --> 11:12.680
Er, this is... I...

11:12.680 --> 11:15.610
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

11:15.610 --> 11:17.190
It's my fault.

11:17.190 --> 11:18.270
Huh?!

11:18.270 --> 11:21.150
Well, I'm a droplet spirit, after all.

11:21.550 --> 11:25.360
When you're close to me, you'll always 
feel as if water's dripping on you.

11:25.360 --> 11:28.580
Oh, that's all it was?!

11:28.580 --> 11:30.700
Well, now we know why...

11:30.700 --> 11:33.330
But why have you been so close to Yufufu?

11:33.820 --> 11:35.830
Well, b-because...

11:36.820 --> 11:39.100
You'll understand when you're older.

11:39.100 --> 11:40.690
Huh...

11:40.690 --> 11:42.600
Grown-ups are so mysterious.

11:42.960 --> 11:46.910
Okay, you two! It's time to head home!

11:47.450 --> 11:49.710
Bye-bye! See you again!

11:49.710 --> 11:50.730
Goodbye.

11:50.730 --> 11:53.980
Yes, please come again anytime.

11:54.190 --> 11:56.100
Sure... Mom.

11:56.690 --> 11:59.250
<i>After living in this world for 300 years,</i>

11:59.250 --> 12:01.900
<i>I now have a mother for the first time.</i>

12:02.490 --> 12:06.000
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

12:06.850 --> 12:09.500
Good morning, Dear Sister!

12:09.760 --> 12:12.490
Have you all been well?

12:12.490 --> 12:15.250
What are all of you doing here?

12:15.550 --> 12:18.880
I mean, I can understand Vania, 
Fatla, and Beelzebub,

12:18.880 --> 12:20.750
but why you, Pecora?

12:21.020 --> 12:25.340
Dear Sister, I've heard about the 
popularity of Slime Snacks.

12:25.340 --> 12:27.630
I hear they're absolutely delicious!

12:27.630 --> 12:30.770
What? Word's spread all the way to Vanzeld?

12:30.770 --> 12:33.110
You've done it again, Dear Sister!

12:33.110 --> 12:35.990
But I will not be outdone!

12:35.990 --> 12:38.280
I baked some cookies!

12:41.280 --> 12:44.370
These are good! 
This can't be just a hobby!

12:44.370 --> 12:45.540
You're a pro!

12:45.540 --> 12:47.720
I did it!

12:47.720 --> 12:50.540
I got Dear Sister's seal of approval!

12:50.540 --> 12:54.280
The Demon King's cookies could 
contend for the best in the world.

12:54.590 --> 12:57.010
I'll keep working hard on them!

12:57.010 --> 12:59.380
Well, I'll be going now.

12:59.380 --> 13:02.370
Wait, this was all you came here for?

13:02.370 --> 13:03.330
Yes!

13:03.330 --> 13:06.130
Do demons have that much 
time on their hands?

13:06.130 --> 13:11.100
Now, hold on. We only stopped by 
because we were nearby on business.

13:11.430 --> 13:12.600
Business?

13:14.690 --> 13:17.710
What? It has to do with me?

13:17.710 --> 13:20.110
It's something somewhat similar to a ghost.

13:20.380 --> 13:22.350
We're searching for undead.

13:22.350 --> 13:25.780
Yes, whether they're demons 
or not is a gray zone,

13:25.780 --> 13:28.120
but they are not overseen 
by the human world,

13:28.120 --> 13:29.990
so the demons look after them.

13:30.430 --> 13:33.660
If an undead is exposed 
as such to the humans,

13:33.660 --> 13:38.810
they would be disgusted or, at worst, 
burn the undead at the stake.

13:38.810 --> 13:40.200
It's a struggle.

13:40.200 --> 13:41.420
Huh...

13:41.420 --> 13:45.520
I know! Why don't we have 
Dear Sister help us?

13:45.520 --> 13:48.680
Why do I have to help?!

13:48.680 --> 13:54.090
If the undead is found by a human 
first, they might be killed.

13:54.090 --> 13:57.260
It'd be so sad, even if 
they're already dead!

13:57.260 --> 13:59.640
This is so confusing!

13:59.640 --> 14:00.780
Sister!

14:00.780 --> 14:03.340
You don't care if they're killed, 
even if they're already dead?!

14:03.340 --> 14:04.520
How sad...

14:04.820 --> 14:06.520
Not you guys, too!

14:08.080 --> 14:11.540
Okay, fine. You want me to help? I'll help.

14:15.150 --> 14:18.200
So how do we search for undead?

14:18.200 --> 14:21.080
Fatla should be arriving soon.

14:32.400 --> 14:35.890
"Please contact us if you meet any undead.

14:35.890 --> 14:38.060
You will be rewarded."

14:38.350 --> 14:41.300
Weren't you trying to find 
them <i>before</i> humans do?

14:41.700 --> 14:45.160
We couldn't come up with 
any other good ideas.

14:50.670 --> 14:52.020
Fightie?

14:52.020 --> 14:56.630
M-Master! I ran all over the 
land handing out flyers!

14:56.890 --> 14:58.460
Good work.

14:58.460 --> 15:00.630
I think you're relying too 
much on her strength...

15:00.630 --> 15:04.370
No... If I get stronger, 
I can make even more money...

15:04.370 --> 15:07.170
Still obsessed with money, I see.

15:07.630 --> 15:12.740
Anyway, after all this, it's just a matter 
of time before we find the undead.

15:14.660 --> 15:16.800
Nobody has contacted us yet.

15:17.060 --> 15:20.260
What can we do?

15:23.070 --> 15:26.440
How do you identify an undead, anyway?

15:26.440 --> 15:28.690
They never age,

15:28.690 --> 15:31.980
they appear both alive and dead...

15:32.730 --> 15:35.540
Wait, that sounds familiar...

15:36.110 --> 15:39.660
Speaking of rumors, is that one about 
the settlement to the south true?

15:39.970 --> 15:43.290
The one that says they never age?

15:43.290 --> 15:46.170
I heard they're not dead, 
but also not alive.

15:47.690 --> 15:50.830
You guys! I know where the undead are!

15:52.170 --> 15:55.430
Are you sure this is where they are?

15:55.760 --> 16:00.010
Yeah, but I don't know a specific location.

16:00.340 --> 16:03.390
I do know that they like rotten fruit,

16:03.640 --> 16:06.260
but they won't be so simple to...

16:24.420 --> 16:28.120
Pondeli, I've brought you 
some rotting fruit.

16:32.300 --> 16:36.510
Sorry. My schedule's flipped 
from too much gaming.

16:36.510 --> 16:38.830
She has animal ears.

16:38.830 --> 16:40.890
She's cat-type beastfolk.

16:41.190 --> 16:44.060
You live such an irregular 
lifestyle, don't you?

16:44.060 --> 16:45.720
I'm all right.

16:45.720 --> 16:49.400
I eat when I'm hungry and 
sleep when I'm tired.

16:49.400 --> 16:51.900
I'm very true to what's natural!

16:52.140 --> 16:55.910
I feel like I heard that 
line in my past life...

16:55.910 --> 16:57.400
Well, until next time.

16:57.400 --> 16:58.550
Sure!

17:06.000 --> 17:07.700
She won't answer.

17:07.700 --> 17:10.040
Leave this to me.

17:10.040 --> 17:11.760
For types like these...

17:12.210 --> 17:15.970
Delivery! Signature, please!

17:15.970 --> 17:17.400
Coming!

17:17.400 --> 17:20.360
Books are delivered so 
quickly these days...

17:23.480 --> 17:25.620
Wait! What do you want?!

17:25.620 --> 17:26.900
I've been searching for you.

17:27.440 --> 17:29.520
You're the undead, aren't you?

17:29.520 --> 17:31.200
N-No, I'm not!

17:31.200 --> 17:33.520
I'm just a grave security guard!

17:33.820 --> 17:35.520
Grave security guard?

17:35.520 --> 17:40.240
Then let's have someone from the temple 
cast a purifying spell on you.

17:40.240 --> 17:42.410
Then we'll know the truth right away.

17:44.550 --> 17:48.390
I'm sorry. Anything but that, please.

17:48.390 --> 17:51.790
I'll do anything... except work.

17:52.160 --> 17:55.280
<i>Yep. She's definitely 
security for her own home.</i>

18:01.040 --> 18:04.610
My name is Pondeli.

18:04.610 --> 18:07.680
I've been undead for about forty years.

18:07.680 --> 18:10.680
What did you do before you became undead?

18:10.680 --> 18:13.070
I lived alone in the royal capital.

18:13.070 --> 18:17.690
I hated working, so I stayed cooped 
up at home lazing around.

18:18.000 --> 18:21.090
Eventually, even eating became a chore,

18:21.090 --> 18:23.200
and then I starved to death.

18:23.500 --> 18:28.070
After I died, I was lying in 
the moonlight for a while,

18:28.070 --> 18:29.910
and then I became an undead.

18:30.520 --> 18:32.910
But it all worked out!

18:32.910 --> 18:36.870
I now truly have a life where I 
won't die even if I don't work!

18:37.270 --> 18:41.230
And I really do watch over the 
graves from that window.

18:41.680 --> 18:46.730
During that last storm, I made 
sure no gravestones fell over!

18:46.730 --> 18:49.610
So in other words, you do nothing.

18:50.130 --> 18:53.300
I'm quite pleased with the life I have.

18:53.750 --> 18:57.120
There's just one thing I 
find lonely about it...

18:57.790 --> 19:00.840
I don't have anyone to play with anymore.

19:00.840 --> 19:03.870
Everyone else always grows up, you know?

19:04.410 --> 19:09.500
I guess it's only people like 
you who can stay kids forever.

19:09.500 --> 19:13.000
Oh, really? That's all?

19:13.000 --> 19:16.890
All you gotta do is train your body, 
and you won't be lonely!

19:16.890 --> 19:20.380
Muscles are your friends, 
and money is your lover!

19:20.600 --> 19:22.330
You are despicable!

19:22.330 --> 19:24.960
What Fightie says may be despicable,

19:24.960 --> 19:27.680
but her "that's all?" comment was accurate.

19:27.680 --> 19:28.260
Huh?

19:28.260 --> 19:30.460
But you need not worry any longer.

19:32.310 --> 19:35.770
We will be your neighbors from now on.

19:36.160 --> 19:36.890
Huh?

19:37.200 --> 19:41.360
You will move to the Fortress City 
Vanzeld in the Demon Realm.

19:41.700 --> 19:44.660
Undead must live in the 
custody of the demons.

19:46.130 --> 19:49.200
You will be able to make 
some demon friends there.

19:49.200 --> 19:51.790
And you can game all you want on days off.

19:51.790 --> 19:53.000
Days off?!

19:53.000 --> 19:57.280
The existence of days off implies 
that I'll have to work!

19:57.700 --> 20:00.040
I absolutely refuse to work!

20:01.050 --> 20:03.010
We're getting nowhere here...

20:03.760 --> 20:06.060
Then let us have a gaming showdown!

20:06.060 --> 20:08.560
Ooh, I get to game?!

20:08.560 --> 20:12.290
But if I win, you must do as I say.

20:12.290 --> 20:15.070
Of course! I'm not gonna lose!

20:15.590 --> 20:19.820
On my pride as a demon, 
I will not lose to an undead!

20:21.520 --> 20:24.290
Yay! I win!

20:24.290 --> 20:27.040
Urgh... I lost...

20:27.270 --> 20:28.290
You suck at this.

20:28.550 --> 20:31.970
I will take you back to the 
Demon Realm, whatever it takes!

20:31.970 --> 20:36.120
Not a chance! I absolutely refuse to work!

20:36.120 --> 20:38.870
Um, how about this?

20:38.870 --> 20:40.040
What?

20:40.630 --> 20:43.010
Pondeli moves to the Demon Realm

20:43.010 --> 20:46.000
and opens a shop where 
she games with people.

20:46.270 --> 20:48.200
A shop for gaming with people?

20:48.200 --> 20:51.200
You want to play games with others, right?

20:51.950 --> 20:57.770
I'm sure there are demons who want 
to game with someone else, too.

20:58.170 --> 20:59.370
I see!

20:59.370 --> 21:03.600
And if lots of people come to play, 
I can make money playing,

21:03.600 --> 21:06.490
but if nobody comes, I don't have to work!

21:06.800 --> 21:09.740
What do you say to that, Beelzebub?

21:11.580 --> 21:14.750
The demons have always been 
on the undead's side.

21:15.440 --> 21:18.630
If it will convince Pondeli 
to come to the Demon Realm,

21:18.630 --> 21:20.590
of course I will accept that.

21:21.090 --> 21:22.750
Sounds good, right, Pondeli?

21:23.130 --> 21:25.510
Yes! Thank you so much!

21:26.080 --> 21:30.030
Now that that's settled, 
we must set a date for your move.

21:30.030 --> 21:31.260
Uh, but...

21:31.530 --> 21:34.530
Moving is a ton of work, isn't it?

21:34.530 --> 21:36.810
At least do that much by yourself!

21:36.810 --> 21:37.810
Right...

23:09.990 --> 23:12.490
<b>Days in the Highlands</b>

23:10.820 --> 23:12.490
Days in the Highlands!

23:12.490 --> 23:15.860
Undead! I know you're in there!

23:15.860 --> 23:18.000
Come out quietly!

23:23.470 --> 23:25.870
There are this many of them?!

23:25.880 --> 23:27.630
<b>Part 2</b>

23:26.180 --> 23:27.620
Part 2!

23:27.990 --> 23:30.880
I've been searching for you! 
You're the undead!

23:30.880 --> 23:34.380
No! I'm not undead!

23:34.380 --> 23:39.780
Undead wanted!

23:37.000 --> 23:39.780
What's her deal?
